            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-57432-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-57432 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Perl versions through 5.43.10 have an integer overflow in S_measure_struct leading to an out-of-bounds heap read in pack and unpack.\n\nS_measure_struct adds each item's size times its repeat count to a running total with no overflow check, so a large repeat count in a pack or unpack template wraps the signed SSize_t total negative. The @, X, and x position codes then guard their moves with a signed length comparison that passes when the length is negative, advancing the buffer pointer out of bounds.\n\nA template derived from untrusted input can read heap memory past the buffer and return it to the caller."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-57432",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-57432\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.34.0-3ubuntu1.7\nFix Version: 5.34.0-3ubuntu1.8\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-57432](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-57432)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-57432**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.34.0-3ubuntu1.7  | 5.34.0-3ubuntu1.8  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04  | [CVE-2026-57432](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-57432)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.34.0-3ubuntu1.7?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-22.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.4"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-6791-libc-bin",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-6791 medium vulnerability for libc-bin package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When expanding paths that begin with a tilde (~) followed by a username, the internal parse_tilde function extracts the username to determine the user's home directory.  The implementation allocates memory for this username directly on the stack using the strndupa macro. Because the size of this allocation was determined by the length of the user-supplied input without any bounds checks, passing an excessively long username e.g. thousands of characters, forces the thread to exhaust its stack space. Thus if an application passes untrusted, attacker-controlled input to the wordexp function, an attacker can trigger a stack clash."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-6791",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-6791\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libc-bin\nVersion: 2.35-0ubuntu3.14\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-6791](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-6791)",
